blocks.en:
We label each image along four dimensions that move from scene content to perceptual impact:
(i) Semantic Description , the intended subject and a natural-language account of scene content, layout, and lighting;
(ii) Global Quality Assessment , the primary distortion plus severity ratings for all six canonical types;
(iii) Local Distortion Analysis , each active distortion’s spatial scope ( Global or Local ) and affected regions;
and (iv) Holistic Quality Narrative , content-impact statements on how active distortions affect perceptual quality and scene understanding. The full annotation schema and field definitions are given in Supp. Sec. A.

